{
  "summary": "Ensures file descriptors and handles opened via fsbridge::fopen are marked close-on-exec and non-inheritable. It appends the 'e' mode character on Linux, appends 'N' on Windows, and falls back on other POSIX platforms to open() with O_CLOEXEC followed by fdopen(). A unit test is added to verify that open file descriptors lack inheritance flags.",
  "problem": "Files opened via fsbridge::fopen can remain inheritable across process boundaries, risking descriptor or handle leaks into child processes spawned by Bitcoin Core (such as via notification scripts or external signers).",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"Use the 'e' mode on POSIX to set close-on-exec and the 'N' mode on windows to prevent file handle inheritance by child processes.\""
  ],
