  "card": "Makes files opened with fsbridge::fopen non-inheritable across process boundaries by appending 'e' on Linux, 'N' on Windows, and falling back to open() with O_CLOEXEC and fdopen() on other platforms. This prevents file descriptors from leaking into spawned child processes like alert or wallet notification scripts. No issue or bug report is linked, and the author cites general hygiene for process handle inheritance.",
